<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sergius VII of Naples</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1137</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sergius VII (d. 1137) was the last independent Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a>, ruling from the early 1120s. He opposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roger-ii-of-sicily">Roger II of Sicily</a> and resisted a long siege of Naples in 1135–1137, but then made peace and submitted to him. He was killed fighting for Roger at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-rignano">Battle of Rignano</a> in 1137, after which Naples was absorbed into the Norman Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>.</p></div>
